          "body": "| Expression | Meaning | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| be charged with | be officially accused of | She was charged with a drug-related offence. |\n| plead guilty | formally admit guilt in court | He refused to plead guilty. |\n| proclaim your innocence | say clearly that you are innocent | She continued to proclaim her innocence. |\n| appeal a sentence | ask a higher court to review a punishment | Her lawyer advised her to appeal the sentence. |\n| a suspended sentence | a prison sentence that is not immediately served if conditions are met | The court imposed a suspended sentence. |\n| a wrongful conviction | a conviction of someone who should not have been convicted | New evidence exposed a wrongful conviction. |\n| carry out a crime | perform a criminal act | The evidence showed who had carried out the crime. |\n| bring someone to justice | make someone face the legal process for what they did | Investigators worked to bring those responsible to justice. |\n\n**Arrested**, **charged** and **convicted** describe different stages. An arrest does not establish guilt. In the story based on *American Violet*, Dee Roberts is accused on weak evidence and has to decide whether to accept a deal or fight the charge.",
