          "body": "| Pattern | Example | Function |\n|---|---|---|\n| It + be + adjective + to-infinitive | It is important to check the evidence. | Gives an evaluation before the action. |\n| It + be + adjective + clause | It is surprising that nobody checked. | Gives a reaction before the fact. |\n| It + seems/appears + that | It appears that someone made a mistake. | Makes a cautious inference. |\n| It + be + past participle + that | It has been reported that the case was reopened. | Reports information without naming the source. |\n| verb + it + complement/clause | I find it hard to believe. / I’d appreciate it if you could help. | Introduces a later clause or infinitive. |\n| fixed expressions | It’s no wonder. / We made it. / I can’t help it. | Learn the expression as a chunk. |\n\nUse *it* for time, weather and distance too: *It’s late. It’s raining. It’s five miles away.* Compare *It seems that he left* with *He seems to have left*. When speaking, divide a long sentence into meaning groups: *The court reopened the case / after new evidence came to light.*",
